1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:02,719
This is NSE Alpha Lab,

2
00:00:02,848 --> 00:00:08,014
an open-source research workspace for testing
momentum rotation strategies on Indian equities.

3
00:00:08,350 --> 00:00:11,846
In the next few minutes, I'll show
you what it does, how to set it up,

4
00:00:11,876 --> 00:00:14,117
and how to write and test your first alpha.

5
00:00:15,630 --> 00:00:18,475
Most backtests are optimistic by accident.

6
00:00:18,809 --> 00:00:23,189
They use today's index members, fill
at the close that produced the signal,

7
00:00:23,219 --> 00:00:25,201
and treat charges as a footnote.

8
00:00:25,563 --> 00:00:28,122
This lab makes those choices explicit.

9
00:00:28,483 --> 00:00:29,851
In the research harness,

10
00:00:29,886 --> 00:00:34,120
membership is applied as of each
rebalance date from official snapshots.

11
00:00:34,237 --> 00:00:37,839
After 2022 those are irregular official anchors,

12
00:00:37,869 --> 00:00:40,016
with coverage between them marked unknown.

13
00:00:40,361 --> 00:00:44,548
The command line records the universe
label, but does not re-filter.

14
00:00:44,881 --> 00:00:49,492
A signal formed on the close of day
T can only fill at the open of T+1.

15
00:00:49,853 --> 00:00:53,556
Every trade pays brokerage, STT, exchange fees,

16
00:00:53,638 --> 00:00:56,056
GST on brokerage, and slippage.

17
00:00:56,139 --> 00:00:58,546
Stamp duty is charged on buys only,

18
00:00:58,698 --> 00:01:03,145
and the rates are 2026-style
constants, not the historical schedule.

19
00:01:04,220 --> 00:01:06,287
The repository is a pipeline.

20
00:01:06,597 --> 00:01:10,796
A private, checksummed data pack
supplies split-and-bonus-adjusted bars.

21
00:01:10,913 --> 00:01:14,275
The research harness joins
point-in-time membership to them.

22
00:01:14,633 --> 00:01:19,680
The full point-in-time NIFTY 500 membership
chain behind the headline is not public.

23
00:01:20,031 --> 00:01:23,817
The canonical engine ranks
trailing returns, holds the top N,

24
00:01:23,958 --> 00:01:26,010
and executes at the next open.

25
00:01:26,363 --> 00:01:29,252
The research report adds beta, Jensen's alpha,

26
00:01:29,605 --> 00:01:34,028
Newey-West t-statistics, and a
block-bootstrap p-value for the headline.

27
00:01:34,381 --> 00:01:39,103
The 968-row table carries beta,
alpha, and both t-statistics,

28
00:01:39,133 --> 00:01:41,068
but not the bootstrap p-value.

29
00:01:41,413 --> 00:01:44,425
And all 968 sweep rows are published,

30
00:01:44,455 --> 00:01:46,342
including the rows that say no.

31
00:01:47,433 --> 00:01:50,487
Setup is quick if you only
want the code and tests.

32
00:01:50,853 --> 00:01:55,240
Clone the repository, sync with
uv, and run the test suite.

33
00:01:55,581 --> 00:01:58,317
The suite is offline and needs no data pack.

34
00:01:58,673 --> 00:02:02,470
For the research UI, install the
lab extra and launch Streamlit.

35
00:02:02,555 --> 00:02:06,825
Its pack detector does not yet
recognise the 1.0.0 layout,

36
00:02:06,836 --> 00:02:09,195
so use the CLI for a real pack.

37
00:02:09,553 --> 00:02:14,129
To run a real backtest, request
access to the private pack, verify it,

38
00:02:14,470 --> 00:02:18,551
then point the command line
at it with NSE_DATA_DIR,

39
00:02:18,892 --> 00:02:21,381
or by placing it in the local data directory.

40
00:02:21,733 --> 00:02:25,377
Verification refuses to
continue on a hash mismatch.

41
00:02:26,450 --> 00:02:29,933
An alpha here is a specification, not a class.

42
00:02:30,283 --> 00:02:34,257
You label the universe, declare
the holding count, the lookback,

43
00:02:34,457 --> 00:02:37,052
the cadence, and any exit overlay.

44
00:02:37,391 --> 00:02:42,144
The spec is explicit; charge rates
and starting cash are fixed constants.

45
00:02:42,470 --> 00:02:46,280
An unknown field is an error,
never silently ignored.

46
00:02:46,643 --> 00:02:49,903
This is the pre-specified primary: NIFTY 500,

47
00:02:49,933 --> 00:02:54,195
the top 10 by 63-session momentum,
monthly cadence, next-open fills,

48
00:02:54,225 --> 00:02:55,806
and the full charge stack.

49
00:02:56,151 --> 00:02:59,258
The published run rebalances
on membership evidence dates,

50
00:02:59,288 --> 00:03:03,415
so after 2022 it is event-anchored
rather than strictly monthly.

51
00:03:04,473 --> 00:03:06,973
Run one spec with the backtest command.

52
00:03:07,301 --> 00:03:10,792
The command line runs the engine
over the bars in the pack.

53
00:03:11,131 --> 00:03:15,412
The published study applies point-in-time
membership in its research harness.

54
00:03:15,751 --> 00:03:19,365
You get sessions, rebalances,
trades, skips, final cash,

55
00:03:19,395 --> 00:03:20,622
and final equity.

56
00:03:20,983 --> 00:03:25,410
Add the out flag, and the full equity
curve, every trade, every exit,

57
00:03:25,440 --> 00:03:27,787
and every skip are written as JSON.

58
00:03:28,154 --> 00:03:30,742
The run in this shot uses
a small synthetic pack,

59
00:03:30,772 --> 00:03:34,794
so you can see the mechanics
without the 161 MB data pack.

60
00:03:35,130 --> 00:03:39,352
It is labelled synthetic on screen,
and it is not a research result.

61
00:03:40,430 --> 00:03:42,591
Testing happens at three levels.

62
00:03:42,943 --> 00:03:47,582
Targeted tests pin the engine's causality
and accounting: next-open fills,

63
00:03:47,612 --> 00:03:49,618
charge sums, and no look-ahead.

64
00:03:49,951 --> 00:03:53,053
The full suite runs offline on frozen fixtures.

65
00:03:53,403 --> 00:03:57,472
A separate validation harness
records 348 fail-closed checks,

66
00:03:57,518 --> 00:04:02,288
including 36 independent recomputations
of beta, alpha, tracking error,

67
00:04:02,318 --> 00:04:04,193
and OLS t-statistics.

68
00:04:04,299 --> 00:04:07,766
The rest are contract and
CSV consistency checks.

69
00:04:08,111 --> 00:04:12,887
The last published run records
348 checks, 0 failures.

70
00:04:13,243 --> 00:04:16,156
The harness checks every published
row's accounting identities,

71
00:04:16,368 --> 00:04:19,918
cross checks the six headline
rows against the published CSV,

72
00:04:20,165 --> 00:04:23,102
and recomputes the alpha
regressions from aligned returns.

73
00:04:23,186 --> 00:04:25,156
Any mismatch fails the run.

74
00:04:26,220 --> 00:04:29,159
And here is the part most repositories hide.

75
00:04:29,523 --> 00:04:33,077
On a price-only basis, net
of the full charge stack,

76
00:04:33,107 --> 00:04:36,846
the pre-specified strategy compounded at 19.3%.

77
00:04:37,204 --> 00:04:40,405
On the benchmark-aligned sessions
used for the alpha regression,

78
00:04:40,435 --> 00:04:42,346
19.45%.

79
00:04:42,703 --> 00:04:46,099
Its Newey-West alpha t-statistic is 1.62,

80
00:04:46,500 --> 00:04:49,142
the OLS t is 1.67,

81
00:04:49,436 --> 00:04:53,493
and its block-bootstrap p-value is 0.096.

82
00:04:53,841 --> 00:04:56,023
Not statistically significant.

83
00:04:56,383 --> 00:04:57,591
Across the sweep,

84
00:04:57,621 --> 00:05:02,810
the median configuration lost to
the NIFTY 50 by 9.73 pp a year.

85
00:05:03,163 --> 00:05:08,588
Only 26 of 968 rows have a
positive Newey-West t above 1.96,

86
00:05:08,752 --> 00:05:10,946
about the 24 expected by chance,

87
00:05:10,969 --> 00:05:13,647
while another 43 are significantly negative.

88
00:05:14,003 --> 00:05:16,574
The highest Sharpe is 1.3362,

89
00:05:16,609 --> 00:05:21,838
the maximum of 968 trials over
windows as short as 4.66 years,

90
00:05:21,868 --> 00:05:22,989
not an expectation.

91
00:05:24,213 --> 00:05:28,647
The tutorial, architecture notes,
the full 968-row results table,

92
00:05:28,682 --> 00:05:31,147
and the disclaimer are in the repository.

93
00:05:31,481 --> 00:05:35,455
The study's JSON inputs and
verification payload are not public,

94
00:05:35,679 --> 00:05:38,958
so read What is reproducible
before you try to rerun it.

95
00:05:39,270 --> 00:05:40,792
If you use it, cite it.

96
00:05:41,329 --> 00:05:43,735
And remember, this is research software.

97
00:05:44,049 --> 00:05:45,818
It is not investment advice,

98
00:05:45,830 --> 00:05:48,991
and past performance does
not predict future returns.
